# React Frontend Patterns

## Component Structure

- Functional components only — no class components
- One component per file, filename matches component name (PascalCase)
- Props defined with TypeScript interfaces, not inline types
- Extract reusable logic into custom hooks in `hooks/`

## Styling

- TailwindCSS for all styling — no CSS modules or styled-components
- Use semantic color variables via Tailwind config (e.g., `text-profit`, `text-loss`)
- Responsive: mobile-first with `sm:`, `md:`, `lg:` breakpoints

## State Management

- Local state with `useState` / `useReducer`
- Server state via React Query (`@tanstack/react-query`) for REST API data
- WebSocket data through custom `useWebSocket` hook — not stored in global state

## WebSocket Pattern

```tsx
const { data, status } = useWebSocket<TickerUpdate>("ws://localhost:8000/ws/ticker");
```

- Reconnect automatically on disconnect
- Parse incoming JSON, validate shape before updating state
- Show connection status indicator in the UI

## Charts

- Use TradingView Lightweight Charts for price/candlestick charts
- Use Recharts for PnL, portfolio allocation, and other dashboard charts
- Charts must handle empty/loading states gracefully
